// Crawly Frontier API: shared task types.
//
// The Frontier API is split into versioned packages, one per role:
//   crawly.frontier.worker.v1  - WorkerService: spiders lease tasks, report outcomes, add discovered tasks.
//   crawly.frontier.run.v1     - RunService: schedulers create, seed, seal, pause and cancel runs; observe them.
//   crawly.frontier.policy.v1  - PolicyService: read-only view of the global policies and how they resolve.
//   crawly.frontier.queue.v1   - QueueService: operators inspect and control queues.
//   crawly.frontier.task.v1    - this package: task types shared by the worker and run APIs. No service.
//
// Core model:
//   Queue  - identified by an opaque, GLOBAL key (usually a host). Owns the limiter. Shared by all runs.
//   Run    - a bounded unit of work with its own budget, stats and policy overrides. Dedup is per run
//            and queue. A run is a dimension on tasks, never a namespace for queues.
//   Task   - one request to fetch, belonging to exactly one run and one queue.
//   Lease  - one dispatch of a task to a worker (an attempt), fenced by lease id and attempt.

